window.OF_SEARCH = [{"title": "Overview", "heading": "", "text": "FileExp is a file manager for Windows and Linux. It runs as a small desktop made only for files: you browse, search, organise, protect and share your files without leaving one window. It needs no internet, has no adverts or accounts, and keeps everything it learns about your files on your own computer.", "url": "en/docs/index.html"}, {"title": "Overview", "heading": "What makes it different", "text": "Undo for everything Rename, move, delete, paste, compress, extract — Ctrl+Z puts it back. Nothing is ever lost by an undo. Timeline A day-by-day diary of what you did with your files, including files changed by other programs. Search with filters type:image size>2mb modified:week , or search inside files with content:\"invoice\" . Tags and smart collections Coloured tags that follow the files when they move; saved searches that are always up to date. Disk health What fills your disk, a folder map, large old files and duplicate files by content. Vault An encrypted folder (AES-256) for private fil", "url": "en/docs/index.html#what-makes-it-different"}, {"title": "Overview", "heading": "How this documentation is organised", "text": "User guide — from installing to every feature, with screenshots. Start with [Installing and first run](install.md), then [My Files](my-files.md). Reference — [all the settings](settings.md), [keyboard shortcuts](shortcuts.md), [your data and privacy](data-privacy.md) and [troubleshooting](troubleshooting.md). Developer guide — [architecture](architecture.md), [building and testing](building.md), [conventions](conventions.md) and [translations](translations.md). Future versions — [roadmap and guidelines](roadmap.md), [how to publish a release](releasing.md) and the [version history](history.md)", "url": "en/docs/index.html#how-this-documentation-is-organised"}, {"title": "Overview", "heading": "At a glance", "text": "Current version 3.11.2 (November 2026) Systems Windows 10/11 (installer and portable app), Linux ( .deb package) Languages of the app English, Português, Español, Français, Deutsch, Italiano, Русский, 日本語, 中文 Made with Java 17 and JavaFX 17, no external libraries File engine Built with OctopusFile Publisher Muendu Studio · Powered by Wonetino Group and Muendu Studio Tip: press / (or Ctrl+K) on any page of this site to search the documentation.", "url": "en/docs/index.html#at-a-glance"}, {"title": "Installing and first run", "heading": "Windows", "text": "Run FileExp-3.11.2.exe . Choose the folder (the default is fine) and whether you want a shortcut on the desktop. The installer also adds FileExp to the Start menu. Open FileExp from the Start menu. There is also a portable version: the folder FileExp with FileExp.exe inside. Copy the whole folder anywhere (even a USB drive) and run FileExp.exe . It brings its own Java, so nothing else has to be installed.", "url": "en/docs/install.html#windows"}, {"title": "Installing and first run", "heading": "Linux (Ubuntu, Debian and derivatives)", "text": "sudo apt install ./fileexp_3.11.2-1_amd64.deb FileExp then appears in the applications menu. On Linux the user folders come from ~/.config/user-dirs.dirs , so translated names such as \"Transferências\" are recognised, and drives mounted in /media , /run/media and /mnt appear in Computer .", "url": "en/docs/install.html#linux-ubuntu-debian-and-derivatives"}, {"title": "Installing and first run", "heading": "Requirements", "text": "System Windows 10 or 11 (64-bit), or a 64-bit Linux with a graphical desktop Memory 4 GB of RAM (FileExp itself uses about 200–400 MB) Disk about 150 MB for the app; your data uses a few MB Java none — the installer and the portable app include their own runtime", "url": "en/docs/install.html#requirements"}, {"title": "Installing and first run", "heading": "First run", "text": "The start screen shows the FileExp icon, the version and the loading state while your preferences open in the background. The first time, the setup assistant opens (since 3.11), with 10 steps. It works entirely with the keyboard: Tab moves from one control to the next, the arrow keys choose within a group and Enter goes on. 1. Welcome The language (one of nine) 2. Licences and privacy Read and accept the licence of FileExp and the notices of the components it includes (required) 3. About you Your name and the colour of your picture 4. Appearance Theme, accent colour, text size, animations 5. F", "url": "en/docs/install.html#first-run"}, {"title": "Installing and first run", "heading": "Licences", "text": "Step 2 shows, in full and unchanged, the licence of FileExp (Apache License 2.0), that of the OpenJDK Java runtime and of OpenJFX (GNU GPL version 2 with the Classpath Exception) and the notices of the components of JavaFX Media (GStreamer, GLib, libffi, DirectShow). Without accepting, FileExp does not go on: I do not accept: close FileExp quits the application. The acceptance (version and date) is kept on this computer; if the documents change in a future version, FileExp asks again, with that step only. The same texts are always in Settings › About › Licences and legal notices .", "url": "en/docs/install.html#licences"}, {"title": "Installing and first run", "heading": "Opening a folder directly", "text": "You can start FileExp in a given folder by passing it on the command line: FileExp.exe \"D:\\Photos\\2026\"", "url": "en/docs/install.html#opening-a-folder-directly"}, {"title": "Installing and first run", "heading": "Choosing the language", "text": "FileExp follows the language of your system. To change it, open Settings › Language , choose one of the nine languages and press Restart now .", "url": "en/docs/install.html#choosing-the-language"}, {"title": "Installing and first run", "heading": "Uninstalling", "text": "Windows: Settings › Apps › FileExp › Uninstall. Your data in %USERPROFILE%\\.fileexp (and the Trash in %USERPROFILE%\\.octopusfile ) is kept; delete those folders if you want to remove everything (see [Your data and privacy](data-privacy.md)). Linux: sudo apt remove fileexp .", "url": "en/docs/install.html#uninstalling"}, {"title": "The desktop", "heading": "", "text": "FileExp opens a full-screen desktop dedicated to files. Everything — menus, dialogs, previews — is drawn inside this one window, with the same theme, so nothing opens on top in a different style.", "url": "en/docs/desktop.html"}, {"title": "The desktop", "heading": "Top bar", "text": "My Files Opens the file browser (also Ctrl+Space ). Clock and date Click to open a calendar. Search Opens My Files with the cursor in the search box. Trash Opens the Trash. Bell Notifications, with a counter of the new ones. Gear Settings (also Ctrl+, ). Avatar Your account, favourites, lock and quit. Power Lock ( Ctrl+Alt+L ), full screen ( F11 ) and quit.", "url": "en/docs/desktop.html#top-bar"}, {"title": "The desktop", "heading": "Widgets", "text": "On the left of the desktop: Clock with the date and a greeting; rings for CPU, memory, disk and Trash, with real values; storage of each drive with a usage bar; recent files and folders. The style of the widgets — Glass, Solid, Minimal, Outline or Accent colour — is chosen in Settings › Desktop , with a preview.", "url": "en/docs/desktop.html#widgets"}, {"title": "The desktop", "heading": "Notifications", "text": "Operations that take time or that you may want to undo end with a banner in the top-right corner. Many banners have an Undo button, for example after a delete, a rename or a move made by an automation; after a transfer, Open or Show is offered in the transfers panel. Older notifications stay in the list under the bell.", "url": "en/docs/desktop.html#notifications"}, {"title": "The desktop", "heading": "Transfers panel", "text": "Copies, downloads, uploads, backups and files received from nearby computers go through the transfers panel in the bottom-right corner. Each transfer shows the progress in bytes, the speed and the time left, and can be cancelled. The panel can be minimised; when a transfer ends you get Open or Show and a notification. Pause and resume (since 3.10). Each unfinished transfer has a Pause button next to Cancel; it becomes Resume . A paused transfer keeps what it has done (a large copy goes on from the same byte), and a paused transfer that had not started keeps its place in the queue. Some transfe", "url": "en/docs/desktop.html#transfers-panel"}, {"title": "The desktop", "heading": "Lock screen", "text": "Ctrl+Alt+L (or the power menu) shows the lock screen: a blurred wallpaper, the clock and your avatar. Click, or press Enter or Space, to come back.", "url": "en/docs/desktop.html#lock-screen"}, {"title": "The desktop", "heading": "Full screen and quitting", "text": "F11 switches full screen on and off. To quit, use the power menu › Quit ; FileExp asks for confirmation and closes the vault if it is open.", "url": "en/docs/desktop.html#full-screen-and-quitting"}, {"title": "My Files: browsing", "heading": "", "text": "My Files is where all the work with files happens. It opens over the desktop with a blurred background, like an applications menu, and shows folders as large icons.", "url": "en/docs/my-files.html"}, {"title": "My Files: browsing", "heading": "Places", "text": "Overview Favourites, Most opened, Recent, Tags, Smart collections, Folders (Home, Desktop, Documents, Downloads, Pictures, Music, Videos, plus This PC, Timeline, Disk health, Vault and Trash), Drives, Network and Cloud. Any folder Its contents, with thumbnails for images. This PC / Computer The drives with a usage bar, label and free space. USB drives have their own icon. Trash Deleted items: restore, delete forever, empty. Disk health See [Disk health](disk-health.md). Timeline See [Tags, timeline and automations](organize.md). Vault See [Vault](vault.md). Each tag Every file with that tag.", "url": "en/docs/my-files.html#places"}, {"title": "My Files: browsing", "heading": "Toolbar", "text": "From left to right: Back , Forward , Up , Overview , the clickable path (click any part to go there), the search box, New (folder or text document, download from the internet, connect to a server), Paste , View (sort, hidden files, thumbnails, details panel), Split view , Details , Refresh and Close . Tip: type a path in the search box (for example D:\\Projects or ~/Music ) and press Enter to go straight there.", "url": "en/docs/my-files.html#toolbar"}, {"title": "My Files: browsing", "heading": "Selecting", "text": "Select one item Click Add or remove an item Ctrl+click Select a range Shift+click Select everything Ctrl+A Clear the selection Click on an empty area, or Esc Open Double-click or Enter When something is selected, the action bar at the bottom shows Open, Cut, Copy, Rename, Compress, Favourite and Delete (and Restore in the Trash). The status bar on the left shows how many items are selected, the free space, and the Undo / Redo buttons.", "url": "en/docs/my-files.html#selecting"}, {"title": "My Files: browsing", "heading": "Details and properties", "text": "The details panel on the right shows a large preview, the type, size (also of folders, calculated in the background), dates, location and tags of the selected item. Properties (Alt+Enter, or right-click › Properties) opens this panel, organised in sections: General — readable type (for example \"PDF document\"), exact size in bytes, contents of a folder, image dimensions, a text preview; Dates — created, modified, last accessed; Advanced — attributes, owner, POSIX permissions, the drive and its file system, and a Calculate SHA-256 button; for drives , General and Space — type (local or removable", "url": "en/docs/my-files.html#details-and-properties"}, {"title": "My Files: browsing", "heading": "Quick look", "text": "Select a file and press Space to see it without opening another program. Images The picture, fitted to the window Text and code The first 256 KB (also files without a known extension, when they contain text) Audio and video A player with Play/Pause (MP3, WAV, AAC/M4A, MP4/H.264) ZIP, DOCX, XLSX, PPTX, EPUB The list of files inside, without extracting Folders A summary of the contents Use ← → to go to the other files of the folder, Enter to open the file in its program, and Space or Esc to close.", "url": "en/docs/my-files.html#quick-look"}, {"title": "My Files: browsing", "heading": "Tabs", "text": "New tab Ctrl+T Close tab Ctrl+W Next / previous tab Ctrl+Tab / Ctrl+Shift+Tab Open a folder in a new tab Middle-click, or right-click › Open in new tab Each tab keeps its own place, Back/Forward history and search. The tab bar only appears when there are two or more tabs.", "url": "en/docs/my-files.html#tabs"}, {"title": "My Files: browsing", "heading": "Split view", "text": "Press F3 (or the split button in the toolbar) to see a second folder side by side. Drag and drop between the two panels, into a folder, or from other programs into My Files. Shift+F5 copies and Shift+F6 moves the selection to the other panel. Copies go through the transfers panel and can be undone; tags follow the files.", "url": "en/docs/my-files.html#split-view"}, {"title": "My Files: browsing", "heading": "Keeping the folder up to date", "text": "FileExp watches the open folder and refreshes it by itself when something changes (you can turn this off in Settings › Files ). F5 refreshes by hand.", "url": "en/docs/my-files.html#keeping-the-folder-up-to-date"}, {"title": "Working with files", "heading": "Copy, cut and paste", "text": "Select the items, press Ctrl+C (copy) or Ctrl+X (cut), go to the destination and press Ctrl+V . The clipboard is the system's: you can copy in FileExp and paste in another file manager, and the other way round. FileExp never overwrites a file by surprise. If the name already exists, the new item gets a free name such as report - Copy.pdf or photo (2).jpg . Large copies go through the [transfers panel](desktop.md) with progress, speed, time left and Cancel .", "url": "en/docs/file-operations.html#copy-cut-and-paste"}, {"title": "Working with files", "heading": "New folder and new document", "text": "New › Folder (Ctrl+Shift+N) or New › Text document . The new item is selected with its name ready to edit.", "url": "en/docs/file-operations.html#new-folder-and-new-document"}, {"title": "Working with files", "heading": "Rename", "text": "Select one item and press F2 . Changing only upper and lower case (\"photo.jpg\" → \"Photo.JPG\") also works on Windows. FileExp checks the name before renaming: empty names, characters such as \\ / : ? \" < > on Windows, names ending with a dot or space, and reserved names ( CON , NUL …) are refused with a clear message.", "url": "en/docs/file-operations.html#rename"}, {"title": "Working with files", "heading": "Rename many items at once", "text": "Select several items and press F2 . Template Holiday {n} → Holiday 1, Holiday 2… (Holiday 01, Holiday 02… with 10 or more items) · {date} {name} → 2026-11-17 report Find and replace Plain text or a regular expression, with or without matching case Prefix and suffix Text added before or after the name Letters Keep letters, lowercase, UPPERCASE or Title Case Include the extension Off by default, so .jpg stays .jpg {name} is the current name, {n} a number, padded with zeros to the width of the largest one (the first number is chosen next to the template) and {date} the date the file was modified.", "url": "en/docs/file-operations.html#rename-many-items-at-once"}, {"title": "Working with files", "heading": "Delete", "text": "Move to Trash Delete The item goes to the FileExp Trash and can be restored or undone. Delete permanently Shift+Delete Removed for good, after a confirmation. The Trash of FileExp works the same on Windows, Linux and macOS. Open it from the top bar or from My Files to restore items to where they were, delete forever or empty the Trash. You can ask FileExp not to confirm before moving to the Trash in Settings › Files .", "url": "en/docs/file-operations.html#delete"}, {"title": "Working with files", "heading": "Undo and redo", "text": "Ctrl+Z undoes and Ctrl+Y (or Ctrl+Shift+Z) redoes. The status bar and the menu of the folder background show the name of the operation, for example \"Undo: Rename 6 items\". Undo covers: rename (also many at once), move to Trash, paste, move, Send to, new folder, new document, compress, extract, moving to the other panel and the moves made by automations. The last 50 operations are kept. An undo never deletes anything for good. What has to disappear (a copy, a new folder) goes to the Trash, and a redo brings it back.", "url": "en/docs/file-operations.html#undo-and-redo"}, {"title": "Working with files", "heading": "Compress and extract", "text": "Compress (action bar or right-click) creates a ZIP of the selection. Extract here and Extract to… on a ZIP. A ZIP with a single folder inside is extracted without creating \"Folder/Folder\". Extraction is protected against zip slip : a ZIP cannot write outside the chosen folder.", "url": "en/docs/file-operations.html#compress-and-extract"}, {"title": "Working with files", "heading": "Send to", "text": "Right-click › Send to lists: the system folders and Choose a folder… ; external devices (USB drives, memory cards, external disks); the cloud : synced folders (OneDrive, Google Drive, Dropbox…) and connected WebDAV accounts; Computers nearby , when [Share nearby](share-nearby.md) is on.", "url": "en/docs/file-operations.html#send-to"}, {"title": "Working with files", "heading": "Download from the internet", "text": "New › Download from the internet… asks for an address and downloads the file into the current folder through the transfers panel.", "url": "en/docs/file-operations.html#download-from-the-internet"}, {"title": "Working with files", "heading": "Favourites", "text": "Right-click › Add to Favorites (or the star in the action bar). Favourites appear first in the Overview.", "url": "en/docs/file-operations.html#favourites"}, {"title": "Search and smart collections", "heading": "", "text": "The search box is in the My Files toolbar. It filters the current folder as you type and also looks in the subfolders. In the Overview it searches your whole home folder. Accents and upper case are ignored: relatorio finds \"Relatório\".", "url": "en/docs/search.html"}, {"title": "Search and smart collections", "heading": "Filters", "text": "Filters can be combined with words and with each other, for example invoice type:document modified:month size>200kb . type: type:image type:video type:music type:document type:archive type:code type:app type:folder Items of that kind ext: or . ext:pdf .docx Files with that extension size> size< size>2mb size<500kb size>1gb Files bigger or smaller (kb, mb, gb, tb) modified: modified:today yesterday week month year 2025 old Files changed in that period tag: tag:Work Files with that tag content: content:\"monthly report\" Files that contain the text The filter names also work in Portuguese, Spanish", "url": "en/docs/search.html#filters"}, {"title": "Search and smart collections", "heading": "Searching inside files", "text": "Write content:\"text\" , or search for a name and press the button Search \"…\" inside the files that appears below the results. FileExp shows each file that contains the text and the line where it appears. It reads text files, code, CSV, JSON, XML and similar files, also in old encodings (Latin-1), and Office documents: Word (DOCX), Excel (XLSX), PowerPoint (PPTX) and LibreOffice (ODT, ODS, ODP).", "url": "en/docs/search.html#searching-inside-files"}, {"title": "Search and smart collections", "heading": "The home index", "text": "FileExp builds an index of your home folder in the background, so searches show results instantly instead of walking through the folders each time. The index is updated as files change. Program folders such as .git , AppData , .cache and the data of FileExp itself are skipped.", "url": "en/docs/search.html#the-home-index"}, {"title": "Search and smart collections", "heading": "Smart collections", "text": "A smart collection is a saved search that is always up to date : \"PDFs of this week\", \"Big videos\", tag:Work … Search for what you want, for example type:video size>500mb . Press Save as smart collection and give it a name. The collection appears in the Overview; open it at any time to see the current results. When you have none yet, the Overview offers examples you can create with one click.", "url": "en/docs/search.html#smart-collections"}, {"title": "Tags, timeline and automations", "heading": "Tags", "text": "Tags are coloured labels you put on files and folders, for example Work , Urgent or Personal . Right-click › Tags shows the existing tags and New tag… . You can tag many items at once. Tagged items show coloured dots on their icons, and the tags appear in the details panel. Each tag is a place in My Files that lists everything with that tag. tag:Work works in the [search](search.md) and in smart collections. Tags are kept by FileExp, so they work on any file system and any drive. They follow the files when FileExp renames or moves them, including the moves made by Undo, the split view and auto", "url": "en/docs/organize.html#tags"}, {"title": "Tags, timeline and automations", "heading": "Timeline", "text": "The Timeline (My Files › Folders › Timeline) is a diary of your work with files, day by day. It records when files were opened , changed in any program , created, renamed, moved, copied, downloaded, uploaded to the cloud, backed up, handled by automations, received from a nearby computer and put in the vault. Events are grouped in work sessions : a pause of more than 45 minutes starts a new session. Each session shows a summary by kind and its files. Click to show the file in its folder; double-click to open it. Files that no longer exist appear faded. The last 5 000 events are kept. Settings ", "url": "en/docs/organize.html#timeline"}, {"title": "Tags, timeline and automations", "heading": "Automations", "text": "Automations are rules that tidy folders for you. Open Settings › Automations . A rule has: Folder to watch Downloads Condition Any search words: type:image , .pdf , size>100mb … Minimum age (optional) Only files older than 30 days Action Move to , Copy to , Move to Trash or Add a tag Destination Pictures/{yyyy}-{MM} — the date parts are replaced by the date of the file ( {dd} , {type} and {ext} also work) Ready-made examples: photos and documents from Downloads, old installers to the Trash, sort Downloads by type.", "url": "en/docs/organize.html#automations"}, {"title": "Tags, timeline and automations", "heading": "How they run", "text": "Every 30 seconds, only on the files directly in the folder — never subfolders or hidden files. Downloads in progress are skipped ( .part , .crdownload , and files changed a few seconds ago). Nothing is overwritten: an existing name becomes \"photo (2).jpg\". Moves can be undone with Ctrl+Z, and the notification has an Undo button. Everything an automation does appears in the timeline.", "url": "en/docs/organize.html#how-they-run"}, {"title": "Tags, timeline and automations", "heading": "Sharing collections and rules (since 3.11)", "text": "A smart collection or an automation rule can go to another computer, or to another person, in a small file with the FileExp icon: .fexc A smart collection (the search and the folder it looks in) In My Files, right-click the collection tile (or the background, inside it) › Export collection... .fexr An automation rule (folder, condition, action, target, minimum age) Settings › Automations › Export... on the row of the rule Choose the folder; FileExp writes <name>.fexc or <name>.fexr and never replaces a file that already exists. Opening the file (double click in the system, or in My Files) show", "url": "en/docs/organize.html#sharing-collections-and-rules-since-311"}, {"title": "Disk health", "heading": "", "text": "Disk health (My Files › Folders › Disk health) answers the question \"what is filling my disk?\" and helps you free space safely: everything goes to the Trash first.", "url": "en/docs/disk-health.html"}, {"title": "Disk health", "heading": "Analysing a place", "text": "Under Place to analyse , choose Home or a drive. Press Analyse . The analysis runs in the background; the window stays usable. Drives Use of each drive, red above 90 %. Space by kind of file How much is images, videos, music, documents, archives, code, programs and others. Map of the folders A treemap : each rectangle is a folder or file, its area is its size. Click to go into a folder, right-click to open it. Largest files The biggest files of the analysed place. Large files not changed for 6 months Big files not changed for more than 6 months. Empty folders Folders with nothing inside.", "url": "en/docs/disk-health.html#analysing-a-place"}, {"title": "Disk health", "heading": "Duplicate files", "text": "Press Find duplicate files . Files of 1 MB or more in the chosen place (Home or a drive) are compared by content (size first, then a SHA-256 hash), never only by name. In each group the oldest copy is kept and the others come already marked. Backups made by FileExp are not counted as duplicates.", "url": "en/docs/disk-health.html#duplicate-files"}, {"title": "Disk health", "heading": "Freeing space", "text": "Check the files you no longer need (or keep the automatic marks in duplicates). Press Move to Trash . Ctrl+Z brings them back. The Trash keeps a compressed copy, so the space is only freed when you press Empty the Trash .", "url": "en/docs/disk-health.html#freeing-space"}, {"title": "Backups", "heading": "", "text": "FileExp copies your important folders to another disk, a USB drive or a network folder. Open Settings › Backups , or right-click a folder › Back up this folder… .", "url": "en/docs/backups.html"}, {"title": "Backups", "heading": "Four kinds of backup", "text": "Copy the changes Copies new and changed files. Nothing is deleted in the destination. Keeping everything, even what you deleted from the original. Exact mirror The destination becomes equal to the original, including deletions. An exact second copy. Compressed (ZIP) A dated ZIP each time, keeping the last N versions. Going back to how a folder was some days ago. Versions (since 3.10) Keeps earlier versions of every file, storing only what changed; the last N runs are kept. Can be encrypted. Getting back yesterday's version of one file.", "url": "en/docs/backups.html#four-kinds-of-backup"}, {"title": "Backups", "heading": "Where the copies go", "text": "Always to <destination>/FileExp Backup/<folder> (a Versions backup to <folder> (versions) , a folder of its own). So an exact mirror never deletes other files that are on the destination disk.", "url": "en/docs/backups.html#where-the-copies-go"}, {"title": "Backups", "heading": "Automatic backups", "text": "Turn on Run by itself when the destination is connected in a backup job: it runs by itself when its destination disk or USB drive is plugged in (at most once per hour). You get a notification when it ends.", "url": "en/docs/backups.html#automatic-backups"}, {"title": "Backups", "heading": "While a backup runs", "text": "Progress and Cancel are in the transfers panel. Files in use by another program are skipped without stopping the backup, and counted in the result at the end. Every backup appears in the [timeline](organize.md).", "url": "en/docs/backups.html#while-a-backup-runs"}, {"title": "Backups", "heading": "Previous versions of a file (since 3.10)", "text": "With a Versions backup of a folder, select a file of that folder in My Files: the details panel shows Previous versions . Show previous versions lists each version with its date and size (\"same as now\" marks the current content). For each one: Restore a copy writes the version next to the file as name (version 2026-11-22 10.15).ext . The current file is never replaced. It goes through the transfers panel, can be undone (Ctrl+Z moves the copy to the Trash) and appears in the timeline. Open shows that version without restoring it (from a temporary copy). The backup drive has to be connected. Ver", "url": "en/docs/backups.html#previous-versions-of-a-file-since-310"}, {"title": "Backups", "heading": "Encrypted backups (since 3.10)", "text": "A Versions backup can be encrypted with a password (at least 8 characters, typed twice). Contents, names, sizes and dates are encrypted with AES-256-GCM. The password is kept on this computer, encrypted with the same key as the cloud passwords, so automatic backups can run when the drive is plugged in. There is no way to recover an encrypted backup without its password. Write it down in a safe place. On another computer, a backup imported with the settings asks for its password again.", "url": "en/docs/backups.html#encrypted-backups-since-310"}, {"title": "Backups", "heading": "Restoring", "text": "The copies are ordinary files and folders (or ordinary ZIP files), so you restore by copying them back with My Files — no special tool is needed.", "url": "en/docs/backups.html#restoring"}, {"title": "Cloud, devices and network", "heading": "", "text": "Open Settings › Cloud & Devices to see everything connected to FileExp.", "url": "en/docs/cloud-network.html"}, {"title": "Cloud, devices and network", "heading": "Synced folders", "text": "FileExp finds the folders of the sync programs installed on your computer: OneDrive, Google Drive, Dropbox, iCloud, MEGA, Nextcloud, ownCloud, pCloud, Box and Yandex . They appear in the Overview and in Send to › Cloud . The sync program itself sends the files to the internet.", "url": "en/docs/cloud-network.html#synced-folders"}, {"title": "Cloud, devices and network", "heading": "WebDAV accounts", "text": "Many services and NAS boxes speak WebDAV: Nextcloud, ownCloud, Box, pCloud, Yandex Disk, Koofr, Synology/QNAP and others. Settings › Cloud & Devices › Connect a cloud… . Enter the server address, the user and the password (use an app password when the service offers one). The account appears in My Files. You can browse, open, download, upload, create folders, delete and copy a link. Passwords are stored encrypted on your computer. Without internet, FileExp shows a message instead of freezing.", "url": "en/docs/cloud-network.html#webdav-accounts"}, {"title": "Cloud, devices and network", "heading": "External devices", "text": "USB drives, memory cards and external disks appear in This PC / Computer with their label (for example \"USB DATA (E:)\") and a usage bar, and in Send to › External devices . A backup job can start automatically when its drive is plugged in.", "url": "en/docs/cloud-network.html#external-devices"}, {"title": "Cloud, devices and network", "heading": "Network servers (SMB)", "text": "Connect to a server… (in Settings › Cloud & Devices, in the New menu of My Files or in the Network section of the Overview) accepts: \\\\server\\folder //server/folder smb://user@server/folder The connection is made by your system (Windows: UNC paths and net use ; Linux: gio mount ; macOS: mount volume ). FileExp saves the address, never the password . Saved servers appear in Network in the Overview.", "url": "en/docs/cloud-network.html#network-servers-smb"}, {"title": "Vault", "heading": "", "text": "The vault is an encrypted folder for private files: documents, scans of ID cards, passwords exported from other programs, and so on. Open it from My Files › Folders › Vault .", "url": "en/docs/vault.html"}, {"title": "Vault", "heading": "Creating the vault", "text": "Open Vault and choose a password of at least 6 characters (a long sentence is easier to remember and harder to guess). Confirm it. There is no way to recover the vault without the password. Not even Muendu Studio can open it. Write the password down somewhere safe.", "url": "en/docs/vault.html#creating-the-vault"}, {"title": "Vault", "heading": "Putting files in the vault", "text": "Right-click files › Vault › Move to the vault or Copy to the vault . Inside the open vault, Add a file… and Add a folder… add a copy. Move encrypts the file and then deletes the original for good — it does not go to the Trash, so no unprotected copy is left behind. Copy encrypts a copy and keeps the original.", "url": "en/docs/vault.html#putting-files-in-the-vault"}, {"title": "Vault", "heading": "Using the vault", "text": "Open a file: it is decrypted to a private folder that is emptied when the vault closes. Save a copy… decrypts a file to a folder you choose. Delete removes a file from the vault. Lock closes the vault at once. The vault closes by itself after 10 minutes without use and when FileExp quits.", "url": "en/docs/vault.html#using-the-vault"}, {"title": "Vault", "heading": "How it protects your files", "text": "Cipher AES-256-GCM, in authenticated blocks of 1 MiB Key Derived from your password with PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256, 310 000 iterations Names, sizes and dates Kept in an index that is also encrypted Tampering Cutting, swapping or changing any block is detected and the file is refused Location ~/.fileexp/vault (encrypted), ~/.fileexp/vault-open (only while open)", "url": "en/docs/vault.html#how-it-protects-your-files"}, {"title": "Share nearby", "heading": "", "text": "Send files and folders to another computer with FileExp on the same network — at home, in the office, in a classroom — without internet, cloud or USB drive.", "url": "en/docs/share-nearby.html"}, {"title": "Share nearby", "heading": "Turning it on", "text": "Share nearby is off by default . Turn it on in Settings › Share nearby on both computers. There you can also choose the name others see and the folder where received files go (by default Downloads/FileExp ).", "url": "en/docs/share-nearby.html#turning-it-on"}, {"title": "Share nearby", "heading": "Sending", "text": "Select files or folders. Right-click › Send to and choose the computer under Computers nearby . Both screens show the same 6-digit code . If the codes match, nobody is in the middle of the connection. Compare them before accepting: the code is what protects you. Both computers need FileExp 3.9.0 or newer . A computer with an older FileExp still appears in the list, but sending to it shows \"The other computer has an older version of FileExp\" — update FileExp there.", "url": "en/docs/share-nearby.html#sending"}, {"title": "Share nearby", "heading": "Receiving", "text": "The receiving computer shows who is sending, what, and the code, and you accept or refuse . Without an answer in 2 minutes the transfer is refused. Received names are cleaned (no .. , no drive letters, no Windows device names such as CON ), so a sender cannot write outside the chosen folder. The files must fit in the free space of the folder; otherwise the transfer stops with a clear message. Nothing is overwritten: an existing name becomes \"photo (2).jpg\". Everything appears in the [timeline](organize.md).", "url": "en/docs/share-nearby.html#receiving"}, {"title": "Share nearby", "heading": "Syncing a folder (since 3.10)", "text": "Make a folder on the other computer like a folder of this one, sending only the files that are new or changed there — the second time, almost nothing is sent. On the receiving computer, turn on Settings › Share nearby › Allow folder sync (off by default). On the sending computer, right-click a folder › Sync with and choose the computer. Computers with an older FileExp, or with folder sync off, are shown greyed out. Choose Only copy new and changed files (default) or Mirror (also delete there what is not here) . The receiving computer shows who syncs which folder, the code and where it goes (by", "url": "en/docs/share-nearby.html#syncing-a-folder-since-310"}, {"title": "Share nearby", "heading": "Security", "text": "Discovery UDP broadcast on port 47821, only while the option is on Key exchange X25519, a new key for every transfer; the sender commits to its key (a hash) before seeing the other one, so a computer in the middle cannot search for keys that give the same code Encryption AES-256-GCM with a nonce counter in each direction Confirmation The same 6-digit code on both screens (one chance in a million for an attacker) Limits At most 4 incoming connections at a time; a silent connection is closed after 15 s The first time you turn it on, Windows may ask whether FileExp can use the network. Allow it f", "url": "en/docs/share-nearby.html#security"}, {"title": "Settings", "heading": "", "text": "Open Settings with the gear in the top bar or Ctrl+, . The search box at the top of the list finds a page by any word (\"wallpaper\", \"usb\", \"shortcuts\"…). Changes are saved immediately. Appearance Dark, light or high-contrast style, 9 accent colours, 5 wallpapers or your own picture, text size. Language System language or one of 9 languages, with Restart now . Display Brightness, night light, full screen, animations (also off when the system asks for fewer animations). Desktop Widgets on/off, widget style (Glass, Solid, Minimal, Outline, Accent colour), clock with 24 h and seconds. Files Show h", "url": "en/docs/settings.html"}, {"title": "Settings", "heading": "Resetting", "text": "Settings › Storage › Reset settings puts the preferences of Appearance, Display, Desktop, Files, Notifications and Privacy & History back to the default (language, keyboard shortcuts and Share nearby keep their values). Your files, tags, favourites, history and backups are not touched.", "url": "en/docs/settings.html#resetting"}, {"title": "Settings", "heading": "System (since 3.11)", "text": "Settings › System connects FileExp with your system. Everything is done for your account only, without administrator rights, and can be turned off here at any time. Each switch shows the real state (read in the background: \"Reading...\"); if a change fails, the message appears and the switch goes back to the real state. Copies of the settings (.fexp) A double click on a .fexp opens the import of the settings in FileExp, and the file has the FileExp icon On (by the installer and the assistant) Smart collections (.fexc) A double click adds the collection (see [Sharing collections and rules](organ", "url": "en/docs/settings.html#system-since-311"}, {"title": "Keyboard shortcuts", "heading": "", "text": "Every shortcut of My Files can be changed in Settings › Keyboard : press Change , then the new key combination. FileExp warns you when a combination is already in use. Default restores one shortcut and Restore all shortcuts restores them all. Only the shortcuts you changed are saved.", "url": "en/docs/shortcuts.html"}, {"title": "Keyboard shortcuts", "heading": "My Files", "text": "Open Enter Quick look Space Properties Alt+Enter Back Alt+← or Backspace Forward Alt+→ Up one level Alt+↑ Refresh F5 Search / write a path Ctrl+L or Ctrl+F Rename (many if several are selected) F2 New folder Ctrl+Shift+N Copy Ctrl+C Cut Ctrl+X Paste Ctrl+V Select all Ctrl+A Move to Trash Delete Delete permanently Shift+Delete Undo Ctrl+Z Redo Ctrl+Y or Ctrl+Shift+Z Show hidden files Ctrl+H New tab Ctrl+T Close tab Ctrl+W Next tab Ctrl+Tab Previous tab Ctrl+Shift+Tab Split view F3 Copy to the other panel Shift+F5 Move to the other panel Shift+F6 Close My Files / clear the search Esc While you t", "url": "en/docs/shortcuts.html#my-files"}, {"title": "Keyboard shortcuts", "heading": "Without a mouse", "text": "Everything in FileExp can be done with the keyboard, and a screen reader (Narrator, NVDA, Orca) says what has the focus. Anywhere Tab / Shift+Tab move between the parts of the screen; a ring shows what has the focus (only while you use the keyboard) Files (the grid) Arrows move between files and folders, Home / End go to the first / last; Shift+arrows select several; Enter opens Files Menu key or Shift+F10 opens the menu of the selected item (or of the folder) Menus ↑ / ↓ move, → opens a sub-menu, ← goes back, Enter chooses, Esc closes and the focus goes back where it was Dialogs Tab stays ins", "url": "en/docs/shortcuts.html#without-a-mouse"}, {"title": "Keyboard shortcuts", "heading": "Desktop", "text": "Open My Files Ctrl+Space Settings Ctrl+, Lock Ctrl+Alt+L Full screen F11", "url": "en/docs/shortcuts.html#desktop"}, {"title": "Keyboard shortcuts", "heading": "Quick look", "text": "Previous / next file ← / → Open in its program Enter Close Space or Esc", "url": "en/docs/shortcuts.html#quick-look"}, {"title": "Your data and privacy", "heading": "", "text": "FileExp works offline and keeps everything on your computer. It has no account, no analytics and sends nothing to Muendu Studio. The only network connections are the ones you start: WebDAV accounts, downloads from the internet, network servers and Share nearby.", "url": "en/docs/data-privacy.html"}, {"title": "Your data and privacy", "heading": "Where FileExp keeps its data", "text": "~/.fileexp/data Preferences, your profile, favourites, activity, tags, smart collections, timeline, backup jobs, automations, accounts, network servers ~/.fileexp/keys The key that encrypts the WebDAV passwords ~/.fileexp/vault The encrypted vault ~/.fileexp/transfer Your settings as they were before each import (the last 5), for Undo ~/.fileexp/vault-open Decrypted files, only while the vault is open (emptied when it closes) ~/.fileexp/cache Files opened from cloud accounts ~/.fileexp/logs The error log: fileexp-0.log (newest) to fileexp-4.log , never more than 5 MB ~/.octopusfile/trash The T", "url": "en/docs/data-privacy.html#where-fileexp-keeps-its-data"}, {"title": "Your data and privacy", "heading": "The database", "text": "The data is a small document database made for FileExp: one JSON file per collection ( settings.json , journal.json , tags.json …). Each save writes a temporary file and then renames it, so a power cut cannot leave a half-written file, and the previous version is kept as .bak .", "url": "en/docs/data-privacy.html#the-database"}, {"title": "Your data and privacy", "heading": "What is recorded", "text": "Files and folders you open (count and last time) Most opened and Recent Settings › Privacy & History Timeline (last 5 000 events) The Timeline Settings › Privacy & History › clear history Favourites Overview Settings › Privacy & History › clear favourites WebDAV passwords Connect to your accounts Stored encrypted; remove the account to delete them SMB servers Reconnect Only the address is saved, never the password Errors and warnings (time, what failed, where in the code) Understand a problem later ( Copy report ) Settings › Privacy & History › clear error log The error log never contains the ", "url": "en/docs/data-privacy.html#what-is-recorded"}, {"title": "Your data and privacy", "heading": "Moving to another computer", "text": "Settings › Storage › Copy of the settings takes your personalisation with you. Export… and choose a folder (a USB drive, a cloud folder). FileExp saves FileExp-settings-<date>.fexp . On the other computer (or after reinstalling), Import… and choose that file. FileExp shows what the copy holds — Preferences, Tags, Smart collections, Automations, Favourites, Backups, Network servers, Cloud accounts — with how many of each. Untick what you do not want, then choose: Merge : keeps what you have and adds what is missing (nothing is doubled); Replace : the chosen parts are cleared first, then filled ", "url": "en/docs/data-privacy.html#moving-to-another-computer"}, {"title": "Your data and privacy", "heading": "Accepted licences", "text": "On the first run, the assistant asks you to accept the licence of FileExp and the notices of the components it includes (see [Installation and first run](install.md)). settings.json keeps only the version number of the accepted documents and the date and time ( legalAccepted , legalAcceptedAt ); nothing is sent. The texts are always in Settings › About › Licences and legal notices .", "url": "en/docs/data-privacy.html#accepted-licences"}, {"title": "Your data and privacy", "heading": "Removing everything", "text": "Quit FileExp and delete the folders .fileexp and .octopusfile in your home folder. Warning: this also deletes the vault and the Trash.", "url": "en/docs/data-privacy.html#removing-everything"}, {"title": "Troubleshooting", "heading": "FileExp does not start", "text": "Wait for the start screen to finish: it shows for at least 3.4 seconds while the data opens. If the start screen shows \"Could not start\", note the message; the details are in ~/.fileexp/logs/fileexp-0.log . A damaged data file is restored from its .bak copy; if that also fails, rename the folder ~/.fileexp/data and start again (your files are not affected, only the preferences). On Windows, the portable FileExp.exe must stay inside its folder, next to app and runtime .", "url": "en/docs/troubleshooting.html#fileexp-does-not-start"}, {"title": "Troubleshooting", "heading": "A folder shows \"Access denied\"", "text": "FileExp shows the reason given by the system. Open the folder with an account that has permission, or change the permissions in the folder properties of your system.", "url": "en/docs/troubleshooting.html#a-folder-shows-access-denied"}, {"title": "Troubleshooting", "heading": "The search does not find a file I just created", "text": "The home index updates in the background; a new file normally appears within seconds. Search inside a folder always reads the folder itself. Files in program folders ( AppData , .git , .cache …) are not indexed.", "url": "en/docs/troubleshooting.html#the-search-does-not-find-a-file-i-just-created"}, {"title": "Troubleshooting", "heading": "A copy is slow or stopped", "text": "Open the transfers panel: it shows the speed and the time left. Network drives and USB 2 drives are slower. A transfer can be cancelled; what was already copied stays.", "url": "en/docs/troubleshooting.html#a-copy-is-slow-or-stopped"}, {"title": "Troubleshooting", "heading": "I deleted something by mistake", "text": "Press Ctrl+Z right away, or the Undo button of the notification. Otherwise open the Trash and Restore . Shift+Delete and emptying the Trash cannot be undone.", "url": "en/docs/troubleshooting.html#i-deleted-something-by-mistake"}, {"title": "Troubleshooting", "heading": "The vault does not open", "text": "The password is checked exactly, including upper and lower case and the keyboard layout. There is no recovery without the password.", "url": "en/docs/troubleshooting.html#the-vault-does-not-open"}, {"title": "Troubleshooting", "heading": "Share nearby does not find the other computer", "text": "Both computers need FileExp 3.7 or newer with Share nearby on. They must be on the same network (some guest Wi-Fi networks isolate devices). Allow FileExp on private networks in the Windows firewall.", "url": "en/docs/troubleshooting.html#share-nearby-does-not-find-the-other-computer"}, {"title": "Troubleshooting", "heading": "The text is too small or too big", "text": "Settings › Appearance › Text size.", "url": "en/docs/troubleshooting.html#the-text-is-too-small-or-too-big"}, {"title": "Troubleshooting", "heading": "\"Something went wrong\"", "text": "When an unexpected error happens, FileExp records it and shows the notification Something went wrong — without stopping your work. If the same error repeats, the notification appears at most once every 10 seconds. Nothing is lost: copies, moves and the other operations have their own messages and Undo .", "url": "en/docs/troubleshooting.html#something-went-wrong"}, {"title": "Troubleshooting", "heading": "Reporting a problem", "text": "Press Copy report on the notification, or open Settings › About › Diagnostics › Copy report . Paste it in your message, and describe what you did, what you expected and what happened. The report has the version of FileExp, the system, Java and the last 20 problems, already without personal data (see [Your data and privacy](data-privacy.md)). Read it before you send it if you want: it is plain text.", "url": "en/docs/troubleshooting.html#reporting-a-problem"}, {"title": "Architecture", "heading": "", "text": "FileExp is a JavaFX 17 desktop application written in Java 17, built with NetBeans/Ant. It uses no external libraries : only the JDK, JavaFX and its own internal packages.", "url": "en/docs/architecture.html"}, {"title": "Architecture", "heading": "Packages", "text": "ao.fileexp FileExp — the Application class, the version ( FileExp.VERSION ) and the start-up sequence. ao.fileexp.desktop Everything on screen: DesktopController (desktop, top bar, widgets, notifications), LauncherController (My Files, with its parts — see below), SettingsController , SplashController , and the views DiskHealthView , TimelineView , VaultView , QuickLook , SplitPanel , TransfersPanel , Treemap , plus Overlays / Popover (menus drawn inside the scene), Icon (vector icons usable in FXML), Theme and Ui helpers. ao.fileexp.window Dialogs — confirmations, questions and forms drawn in", "url": "en/docs/architecture.html#packages"}, {"title": "Architecture", "heading": "My Files inside", "text": "LauncherController is the FXML controller of My Files: it owns the nodes, the state (location, items, selection set, history) and the flow — navigation, loading, rendering the tiles, the toolbar and the keys. The rest lives in parts of the same package, each created once by the controller and reaching it through a field lc : SelectionModel Select one, a range (Shift), all, none; keeps the tiles and the details in step FileActions Copy, cut, paste, delete, rename, new folder and text file, ZIP, Send to, Undo/Redo, Trash, and the background runner of these operations ContextMenus Right click on ", "url": "en/docs/architecture.html#my-files-inside"}, {"title": "Architecture", "heading": "Layers", "text": "FXML + controllers (desktop, window) <- what the user sees control (operations, search, rules...) <- logic, testable without a screen data (settings, tags, journal...) <- the user's data, as JavaFX properties store (JSON document collections) <- persistence, atomic writes octopusfile (file engine, JDK only) <- every touch of the file system Rules: the screens call control and data ; control uses octopusfile for all file work; nothing below desktop imports JavaFX controls. The file engine does not know FileExp exists.", "url": "en/docs/architecture.html#layers"}, {"title": "Architecture", "heading": "Start-up", "text": "FileExp.main checks whether this user already has a FileExp open ( control/SingleInstance , since 3.11): if so, it hands over the folders and files of the command line and ends. FileExp.start shows the splash ( Splash.fxml ) — at least 3.4 s for the animation. In the background: DataContext.open() opens the store in ~/.fileexp/data , the language is chosen, the file engine is prepared. Desktop.fxml is loaded and DesktopController.welcome() decides what appears (since 3.11): on the first run , the setup assistant ( desktop/SetupWizard , 10 steps); for someone who already used FileExp but has no", "url": "en/docs/architecture.html#start-up"}, {"title": "Architecture", "heading": "The data store", "text": "ao.fileexp.store keeps collections of JSON documents , one file per collection in ~/.fileexp/data : settings All preferences ( AppSettings turns each into a JavaFX property that saves itself) users Profile and sessions activity Count and last access of opened files and folders favorites Favourites journal Timeline events (last 5 000) tags , tagdefs Tags on files, and tag names/colours collections Smart collections rules Automations backups Backup jobs cloud WebDAV accounts (passwords encrypted) network Saved SMB servers Writes are done in the background, atomically (temporary file + rename) an", "url": "en/docs/architecture.html#the-data-store"}, {"title": "Architecture", "heading": "Threads", "text": "The JavaFX thread only builds and updates the interface. File work runs on background executors (the engine's TransferManager , the index, analyses) and returns with Platform.runLater . Dialogs use a nested event loop ( Dialogs ), so code can ask a question and wait for the answer without blocking the screen.", "url": "en/docs/architecture.html#threads"}, {"title": "Architecture", "heading": "Interface", "text": "One Stage ; everything else (menus, dialogs, previews, windows such as Settings) is drawn in the scene by Overlays , Popover and Dialogs , so it follows the theme and never opens system windows. The FXML files ( Desktop , Launcher , Settings , Splash , InternalWindow ) use the style classes of desktop.css and <Icon name=\"…\" size=\"…\"/> for symbolic icons; Theme puts theme-dark or theme-light on the root, and colours come from desktop.css variables ( -fe-bg , -fe-accent …). Tiles of a folder are drawn in blocks, one block per frame, and tooltips are created only when the mouse is over a tile.", "url": "en/docs/architecture.html#interface"}, {"title": "Building and testing", "heading": "What you need", "text": "JDK 17 C:\\Program Files\\Java\\jdk-17.0.18 JavaFX SDK 17 C:\\Program Files\\Java\\javafx-sdk-17-0-18 (to compile and run) JavaFX jmods 17 C:\\Program Files\\Java\\javafx-jmods-17.0.18 (to package) NetBeans 18 (with its Ant) to open the project WiX Toolset 3.11 only for the Windows installer Python 3 only for translations and the documentation website", "url": "en/docs/building.html#what-you-need"}, {"title": "Building and testing", "heading": "Opening the project", "text": "Open the folder FileExp in NetBeans ( File › Open Project ). It is a standard Ant project ( nbproject/ ); the JavaFX modules are in run.jvmargs in nbproject/project.properties .", "url": "en/docs/building.html#opening-the-project"}, {"title": "Building and testing", "heading": "Building outside the IDE", "text": "NetBeans' own Ant can be used from a terminal. In PowerShell: & \"C:\\Program Files\\NetBeans-18\\netbeans\\extide\\ant\\bin\\ant.bat\" -q \"-Duser.properties.file=$env:APPDATA\\NetBeans\\18\\build.properties\" jar The result is dist/FileExp.jar . Other targets are used the same way (replace jar ): jar Compile and build dist/FileExp.jar run Build and run selftest The automatic tests package-exe dist/package/image/FileExp/FileExp.exe — portable app with its own Java package-installer dist/package/installer/FileExp-x.y.z.exe — Windows installer (needs WiX) package-deb Debian/Ubuntu package (run on Linux, -Dja", "url": "en/docs/building.html#building-outside-the-ide"}, {"title": "Building and testing", "heading": "Automatic tests", "text": "The tests are in selftest/ and use a small test runner made for the project (no JUnit): ant selftest # about half a minute ant selftest -Dselftest.mode=all # also the 50 000-file performance test ant selftest -Dselftest.mode=perf # only the performance test They run with a temporary home folder ( build/selftest/home ), so your real data is never touched. FileOperationsTest Copy, move, rename, Trash, names that must be refused BatchRenamerTest Templates, conflicts, swaps, all-or-nothing UndoHistoryTest Undo/redo of every operation ZipTest Compress, extract, zip slip TransferTest Progress, name ", "url": "en/docs/building.html#automatic-tests"}, {"title": "Building and testing", "heading": "Continuous integration", "text": "Every push and pull request to GitHub runs .github/workflows/ci.yml on Windows and Linux : compile FileExp and run ant selftest ; python i18n/build_tsv.py --check — fails if a text of the code has no translation, or if strings.tsv was not rebuilt; python docs/fileexp/build_site.py — fails if a page or a screenshot exists in one language and not in the other. Every Monday the performance test (50 000 files) runs too; it can also be started by hand in GitHub › Actions › CI › Run workflow. The work is done by ci/ci.py , so you can run exactly the same thing on your computer before you push: pytho", "url": "en/docs/building.html#continuous-integration"}, {"title": "Building and testing", "heading": "Display scaling (125 %, 150 %, 200 %)", "text": "On a 1920x1080 screen, Windows at 200 % leaves only 960x510 logical pixels: that is where layouts break. Check every change that touches the screen with: python tools/scale/scale_check.py # 100, 125, 150 and 200 % (about 4 minutes each) python tools/scale/scale_check.py --scales 2.0 # only the hardest one It opens FileExp with a demo home folder ( build/scale/home , so your own files are never used or shown), goes through the main screens and every Settings page, and saves each one in physical pixels in build/scale/<scale>/ with an audit.txt . The audit lists text cut with \"…\" and anything tha", "url": "en/docs/building.html#display-scaling-125-150-200"}, {"title": "Building and testing", "heading": "Checking the interface without touching your desktop", "text": "For changes on screen, a small harness class can start FileExp with a fake home folder and save images of the scene: java \"-Duser.home=C:\\scratch\\fakehome\" --module-path \"C:\\Program Files\\Java\\javafx-sdk-17-0-18\\lib\" --add-modules javafx.controls,javafx.fxml,javafx.swing,javafx.media -cp \"build\\classes;harness\" MyHarness The harness calls Platform.runLater , drives the controllers and saves scene.snapshot(null) as PNG. Never enable Share nearby or bind to 0.0.0.0 in a harness: it makes the Windows firewall ask the user.", "url": "en/docs/building.html#checking-the-interface-without-touching-your-desktop"}, {"title": "Building and testing", "heading": "The documentation website", "text": "python docs/fileexp/build_site.py # this site (English and Portuguese) It reads the Markdown pages and write plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript to site/ . Open site/index.html directly in a browser.", "url": "en/docs/building.html#the-documentation-website"}, {"title": "Conventions and rules", "heading": "", "text": "These rules keep FileExp coherent from version to version. A change that breaks one of them needs a very good reason, written in the changelog.", "url": "en/docs/conventions.html"}, {"title": "Conventions and rules", "heading": "The non-negotiable rules", "text": "No external libraries. Only the JDK, JavaFX and the project's own packages. Need something (JSON, HTTP, crypto, ZIP)? It is either in the JDK or written in the file engine. NetBeans/Ant project. No Maven or Gradle in the application. Targets are added to build.xml . The user's data goes to the NoSQL store ( ao.fileexp.store ) — never to .properties files, the registry or a separate database. FXML is extended, not rewritten. Add nodes following the existing pattern: the style classes of desktop.css (the theme comes from theme-dark / theme-light on the root), <Icon name=\"..\" size=\"..\"/> for symb", "url": "en/docs/conventions.html#the-non-negotiable-rules"}, {"title": "Conventions and rules", "heading": "Code style", "text": "Java 17, 4 spaces, braces always, one top-level class per file. Names, comments and logs in English . Package-private by default; @Internal on file engine code that is not public API. A class that only holds logic goes to control ; a class that holds user data goes to data .", "url": "en/docs/conventions.html#code-style"}, {"title": "Conventions and rules", "heading": "Performance rules (learned on folders with 50 000 files)", "text": "List folders with Files.walkFileTree at depth 1 (or the engine's listing): attributes come with the listing, not one disk call per file. Never create a Tooltip per tile — each one is a window with its own scene. Create it when the mouse enters. Draw many tiles in blocks, one block per frame. Cache what the system answers slowly (free space, drive labels). Anything that can take more than ~50 ms runs in the background and comes back with Platform.runLater .", "url": "en/docs/conventions.html#performance-rules-learned-on-folders-with-50-000-files"}, {"title": "Conventions and rules", "heading": "Threads and JavaFX", "text": "Touch nodes only on the JavaFX thread. Never block the JavaFX thread on a file operation; use the transfers queue for anything long, so the user sees progress and can cancel. Dialogs uses a nested event loop: do not call it from a background thread.", "url": "en/docs/conventions.html#threads-and-javafx"}, {"title": "Conventions and rules", "heading": "Security rules", "text": "Passwords of accounts are stored encrypted ( CredentialVault ); SMB passwords are never stored. Received or extracted names are cleaned: no .. , no absolute paths, no drive letters. Network features are off by default and bind only to the needed address.", "url": "en/docs/conventions.html#security-rules"}, {"title": "Conventions and rules", "heading": "Tests", "text": "Each feature comes with tests in selftest/ , run with ant selftest before every build that goes to users. Tests use the temporary home folder; they never touch the real one.", "url": "en/docs/conventions.html#tests"}, {"title": "Conventions and rules", "heading": "Changelog", "text": "Every change that a user can notice goes to CHANGELOG.md (in Portuguese), under \"Por publicar\" until the version is released.", "url": "en/docs/conventions.html#changelog"}, {"title": "Translations", "heading": "", "text": "FileExp is translated into 9 languages: English, Portuguese, Spanish, French, German, Italian, Russian, Japanese and Chinese. English is the source language.", "url": "en/docs/translations.html"}, {"title": "Translations", "heading": "How it works", "text": "In Java, every visible text goes through I18n.tr(\"English text\") . In FXML, texts are written in English and I18n.translate(root) translates the loaded tree. Dates use the format of the chosen language. The language is chosen in Settings › Language (\"Same as the system\" by default) and applied on restart.", "url": "en/docs/translations.html#how-it-works"}, {"title": "Translations", "heading": "The translation files", "text": "The texts live in i18n/translations-1.txt … translations-6.txt , one text per line, the 9 languages separated by ‖ : # English ‖ Português ‖ Español ‖ Français ‖ Deutsch ‖ Italiano ‖ Русский ‖ 日本語 ‖ 中文 Move to Trash ‖ Mover para o lixo ‖ Mover a la papelera ‖ Mettre à la corbeille ‖ In den Papierkorb ‖ Sposta nel cestino ‖ В корзину ‖ ごみ箱へ移動 ‖ 移到回收站", "url": "en/docs/translations.html#the-translation-files"}, {"title": "Translations", "heading": "Adding or changing a text", "text": "Write the English text in the code: I18n.tr(\"Back up this folder...\") . Add a line with the 9 translations to one of the translations- .txt files. Generate the table used by the app: python i18n/build_tsv.py It writes src/ao/fileexp/i18n/strings.tsv and lists the texts of the code that still have no translation . Build again and check the screen in at least one other language.", "url": "en/docs/translations.html#adding-or-changing-a-text"}, {"title": "Translations", "heading": "Adding a language", "text": "Add a column to every line of the translations- .txt files (and to the header). Add the language code to LANGS in build_tsv.py and to I18n.LANGUAGES (the list in Settings › Language is built from it). Add the words of the search filters to SearchFilter if the language should have its own ( tipo: , type: …). Check long texts: German and Russian are often 30 % longer than English.", "url": "en/docs/translations.html#adding-a-language"}, {"title": "Translations", "heading": "Style", "text": "Portuguese is European Portuguese (\"ficheiro\", \"Definições\", \"Transferências\"). Use the same word for the same thing everywhere (Trash = Lixo, Undo = Anular). Keep the {0} -style placeholders and the quotes of the English text.", "url": "en/docs/translations.html#style"}, {"title": "Roadmap and guidelines", "heading": "", "text": "This page is for whoever builds the next versions of FileExp. It explains how versions are numbered, what every new feature must bring, how to keep users' data safe across versions, and which directions are planned.", "url": "en/docs/roadmap.html"}, {"title": "Roadmap and guidelines", "heading": "Version numbers", "text": "FileExp uses MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH (for example 3.7.1): MAJOR The way of working changes a lot, or old data needs a one-way migration 3.0.0 — the file manager became a desktop MINOR New features, compatible with the data of the previous version 3.7.0 — tabs, split view, Share nearby PATCH Fixes and small polish, no new data 3.7.1 — new icon and start screen The version lives in FileExp.VERSION (Java) and pkg.version ( build.xml ) — change both.", "url": "en/docs/roadmap.html#version-numbers"}, {"title": "Roadmap and guidelines", "heading": "Definition of done for a new feature", "text": "A feature is finished only when it has: [ ] its logic in control / data (or the file engine), separate from the screen; [ ] all its file work through the file engine, with Undo if it changes files and a timeline event; [ ] all texts through I18n.tr , with the 9 translations, and build_tsv.py reporting nothing missing; [ ] keyboard access (and a configurable shortcut in Shortcuts if it is a frequent action); [ ] search keywords for its Settings page, if it has one; [ ] automatic tests in selftest/ , all passing with ant selftest ; [ ] a page (or section) in this documentation, in English and Po", "url": "en/docs/roadmap.html#definition-of-done-for-a-new-feature"}, {"title": "Roadmap and guidelines", "heading": "Keeping users' data safe between versions", "text": "Every collection file has a version field. When the shape of a document changes, migrate on read : accept the old shape, write the new one, and raise the version. Never remove a field the previous version still reads, within the same MAJOR version. Unknown fields must be kept when a document is saved (a newer version may have written them). New settings must have a default, so an old settings.json keeps working. The .bak copy is the safety net: never delete it automatically. Formats that hold users' files (vault, Trash, backups) change only with a way to read the old format.", "url": "en/docs/roadmap.html#keeping-users-data-safe-between-versions"}, {"title": "Roadmap and guidelines", "heading": "Directions for the next versions", "text": "", "url": "en/docs/roadmap.html#directions-for-the-next-versions"}, {"title": "Roadmap and guidelines", "heading": "3.8 — Reliability and reach (released, 20 Nov 2026)", "text": "Error log, continuous integration, accessibility and high contrast, display scaling, export and import of the settings: all done — see the [version history](history.md).", "url": "en/docs/roadmap.html#38-reliability-and-reach-released-20-nov-2026"}, {"title": "Roadmap and guidelines", "heading": "3.9 — Security (released, 21 Nov 2026)", "text": "Security review of the file engine (OctopusFile 1.3.0): Share nearby protocol 2, crash-safe vault password change, safer saved passwords and SMB on macOS — see the [version history](history.md). 3.9.1 (21 Nov 2026) moved the file engine to OctopusFile 2.0.1 LTS — see the [version history](history.md).", "url": "en/docs/roadmap.html#39-security-released-21-nov-2026"}, {"title": "Roadmap and guidelines", "heading": "3.10 — Power features (released, 22/11/2026)", "text": "File versions restored from the details panel, encrypted backups, folder sync between two computers with Share nearby, pause and resume in the transfers panel, content search in Office documents: all done (file engine OctopusFile 2.1.1) — see the [version history](history.md).", "url": "en/docs/roadmap.html#310-power-features-released-22112026"}, {"title": "Roadmap and guidelines", "heading": "3.11 — First run and system integration (released, 22/11/2026)", "text": "A 10-step setup assistant with the licences, the .fexc and .fexr formats with their own icons, Settings › System and a single instance: all done — see the [version history](history.md). Left for later: terms of use of Muendu Studio (the application already shows them when they exist in legal/terms-<language>.txt ).", "url": "en/docs/roadmap.html#311-first-run-and-system-integration-released-22112026"}, {"title": "Roadmap and guidelines", "heading": "4.0 — Platform", "text": "macOS package and testing. An extensions API inside FileExp (actions in menus, previewers, Settings pages) — still without external libraries. Revisit the window model: optionally open My Files as a normal window for people who do not want the full-screen desktop.", "url": "en/docs/roadmap.html#40-platform"}, {"title": "Roadmap and guidelines", "heading": "Technical debt to pay", "text": "LauncherController had about 3 800 lines — Done in 3.8 : about 1 500 lines plus 10 parts (see [Architecture](architecture.md)) DesktopController is large Same Move widgets and notifications to their own classes No automatic tests of screens Interface regressions are found by hand Turn the screenshot harness into a test target that compares key screens macOS not tested Code paths exist but are unverified Test on a Mac before claiming support CHANGELOG only in Portuguese International users Keep the changelog in Portuguese and the release notes of this site in both languages", "url": "en/docs/roadmap.html#technical-debt-to-pay"}, {"title": "Roadmap and guidelines", "heading": "Things to avoid", "text": "Adding a library \"just for this one thing\". Write the small part needed, in the file engine, with tests. Opening system windows (file choosers, alerts) — use Dialogs . Long work on the JavaFX thread. Network features that are on by default. Deleting users' files without the Trash or a clear, explicit confirmation.", "url": "en/docs/roadmap.html#things-to-avoid"}, {"title": "Publishing a release", "heading": "", "text": "A step-by-step checklist to go from the code to an installer users can trust.", "url": "en/docs/releasing.html"}, {"title": "Publishing a release", "heading": "1. Prepare", "text": "Choose the number (see [Version numbers](roadmap.md)). Change it in src/ao/fileexp/FileExp.java ( VERSION ) and in build.xml ( pkg.version ). Then build from clean : delete build/classes (not ant clean , which also deletes dist/ ). VERSION is a constant that Java copies into the classes that use it (Settings › About, the error report): an incremental build keeps the old number there. In CHANGELOG.md , rename \"Por publicar\" to the version and date, for example ## 3.8.0 (02/12/2026) — Title . Run python i18n/build_tsv.py — it must report no missing translations .", "url": "en/docs/releasing.html#1-prepare"}, {"title": "Publishing a release", "heading": "2. Test", "text": "ant jar ant selftest ant selftest -Dselftest.mode=all Or simply python ci/ci.py --mode all . All tests must pass, and the CI must be green on Windows and Linux for the commit you release (GitHub › Actions). Then check by hand, at least in English and Portuguese: [ ] first run with an empty home (setup assistant, licences, welcome); [ ] browse, copy, rename many, delete, undo, redo; [ ] search with filters and inside files; [ ] quick look of an image, a text and a ZIP; [ ] Settings: every page opens; [ ] the new features of this version. [ ] python tools/scale/scale_check.py reports no problem ", "url": "en/docs/releasing.html#2-test"}, {"title": "Publishing a release", "heading": "3. Package", "text": "ant \"-Dpkg.dir=dist/package-3.8.0\" package-installer Results: dist/package-3.8.0/image/FileExp/ — portable app; dist/package-3.8.0/installer/FileExp-3.8.0.exe — installer. On Linux, ant package-deb -Djavafx.jmods=/path/to/javafx-jmods-17 .", "url": "en/docs/releasing.html#3-package"}, {"title": "Publishing a release", "heading": "4. Check the package", "text": "[ ] Install on a clean user account (or a virtual machine). [ ] The icon, name, version and publisher (Muendu Studio) are right in the installer and in Settings › About. [ ] Start, open a folder, quick look a video (the javafx.media module is included), quit. [ ] Uninstall: the app goes, ~/.fileexp stays.", "url": "en/docs/releasing.html#4-check-the-package"}, {"title": "Publishing a release", "heading": "5. Documentation", "text": "[ ] Update the pages of the new features, in English and Portuguese. [ ] Update the screenshots if screens changed. [ ] Add the version to the [version history](history.md) (both languages). [ ] python docs/fileexp/build_site.py and open the site.", "url": "en/docs/releasing.html#5-documentation"}, {"title": "Publishing a release", "heading": "6. Publish", "text": "[ ] Commit, tag v3.8.0 , push the commit and the tag. The Release workflow creates the GitHub Release with the JAR and the section of the version in CHANGELOG.md . [ ] Attach the installer to that Release: GitHub › Releases › the version › Edit › drag FileExp-<version>.exe from dist/package-<version>/installer/ › Update release — or gh release upload v<version> dist/package-<version>/installer/FileExp-<version>.exe . Since 3.11.3 installers are not kept in git ( dist/package- / is in .gitignore ): an installer is over 50 MB, and GitHub warns about every file that size on push. Files attached t", "url": "en/docs/releasing.html#6-publish"}, {"title": "Version history", "heading": "", "text": "The full, detailed list of changes is in CHANGELOG.md in the project (in Portuguese). This page summarises each version. 3.11.2 22 Nov 2026 Security , second part of the CVE-2026-114938 (\"Java4Shell\") fix: file engine OctopusFile 2.1.2 , and FileExp's own code, decode Base64 only through SafeBase64 , which never uses Java's faulty decoder — FileExp is safe even on a Java that was not updated (the JAR run with the system Java). Same results, formats and data; Share nearby works with 3.9.0 and later. 3.11.1 22 Nov 2026 Security : the Java runtime inside the installer moves from 17.0.18 to 17.0.2", "url": "en/docs/history.html"}];
